e NC State Career Development Center is excited to share that Ashton Poplaski has been selected as the new Rural Outreach Coordinator, where she will lead the center's Rural Works! Program and the SECU Public Fellows Internship Program. July 07, 2026 The NC State University Foundation Grant Supports Expansion of Life Lab Career Readiness Curriculum In partnership with the Office of Undergraduate Research (OUR), the Career Development Center has received a grant from the NC State University Foundation, Inc. to support the growth of NC State’s Life Lab curriculum. April 30, 2026 Mary Smith To Lead Career Development Center Earlier this month, Kesha Reed, Ed.D., associate vice chancellor and associate dean for the Division of Academic and Student Affairs, announced the appointment of Mary Smith, Ph.D. who brings over 20 years of experience in higher education leadership, as the Career Development Center’s new executive director, effective May 4. Career Preparation by the Numbers Data from the Undergraduate Future Plans Survey (AY 2024 to 2025) highlights how NC State students prepare for their careers. 73% Attended a Career Fair 64% Used ePACK 70% Completed an Internship Mission Statement The Career Development Center prepares and empowers students to identify and pursue their career goals. We provide individualized career coaching, help students connect with employers, and offer tools for exploring career paths and building essential job search skills. Latest Stories August 26, 2026 Ashton Poplaski Named New Rural Outreach Coordinator July 18, 2026 Supporting the Neurodivergent Mind Summit July 6, 2026 The NC State University Foundation Grant Supports Expansion of Life Lab Career Readiness Curriculum Career Development Center Home 2100 Pullen Hall 201 Dan Allen Drive Raleigh, NC 27695-7303 [email protected] 919.515.2396 Directions to Pullen Hall About Us Website Accessibility Compliments and Complaints Website Feedback Staff Login Connect With Us Facebook LinkedIn Ins