cape designs to life under the gu... View Details Bookmark Research Assistant 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 111801 - Entomology and Plant Pathology EPS/SAAO No The Research Assistant plays a key role in advancing the Turfgrass Entomology Program’s laboratory, greenhouse, and field research. Working in collaboration with the Principal Investigator (PI), this position independently coordinates multiple concurrent research projects, exercises scientific judgment, and ensures research activities are implemented with quality, accuracy, and efficiency. The ... View Details Bookmark Biotechnology Program Coordinator 23 - University Interdisciplinary Programs 237002 - Biotechnology Teaching SHRA No In this role, you will play a central role in advancing the Biotechnology (BIT) Program and supporting the students, faculty, and partners who make it successful. You will serve as the program expert and a trusted advisor to students, helping them navigate their academic programs, connect with opportunities, and achieve their educational and professional goals.You will work closely with BIT lea... View Details Bookmark Sponsored Research Administrator 14 - College of Engineering 143301 - Engineering Research Administration EPS/SAAO No The College of Engineering is looking to hire multiple Sponsored Research Administrators (SRA) within the newly established college-managed operating model, responsible for orchestrating both pre-award and post-award lifecycles for an assigned departmental faculty portfolio. While the incumbent is physically co-located within a department to provide high-touch, localized customer service, the p... View Details Bookmark Associate Vice Chancellor, Research Administration 06 - Office of Research and Innovation 060401 - ORI-Ofc of Sponsored Programs EPS/SAAO No The Associate Vice Chancellor, Research Administration  (AVC-RA) serves as the university’s senior executive leader for sponsored programs and institutional research administration, providing strategic oversight of enterprise-wide pre-award services, sponsored project administration, research contracts, research administration systems, and research administration data governance. Reporting dire... View Details Bookmark Associate Vice Chancellor, Research Commercialization 06 - Office of Research and Innovation 067401 - ORC - Technology Licensing Office EPS/SAAO No The Associate Vice Chancellor for Research Commercialization (AVC‑RC) provides executive leadership for NC State’s commercialization enterprise, spanning intellectual property management, licensing, startup formation, venture development, and investment programs. The AVC sets university‑wide commercialization strategy, ensures compliance with federal and institutional requirements, and leads pr... View Details Bookmark Research Technician 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 110701 - Animal Science SHRA No Support innovative research in reproductive physiology and molecular biology by providing technical expertise and laboratory support for multiple research programs. As a Research Technician, you will play an essential role in maintaining transgenic mouse colonies, conducting molecular biology experiments, and supporting faculty, students, and scientists in advancing high-quality research. This ... View Details Bookmark Research Technician - Horticultural Science 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 111501 - Horticultural Science SHRA No The Department of Horticultural Science is seeking a motivated and experienced professional to support the day-to-day operations of the Horticulture Field Lab (HFL), a large-scale outdoor and greenhouse research complex serving faculty, students, researchers, and industry partners across multiple departments. The HFL supports a wide range of field and greenhouse research, teaching, extension, a... View Details Bookmark UTS-Temporary Event Preparation Staff 48 - Human Resources 480501 - UHR Temporary Services Temporary No NC State Continuing and Lifelong Education (NCSCaLE) is a division of the Provost within the Office of the Vice Provost for Continuing Education. The McKimmon Conference and Training Center (MCTC) reports to the Continuing & Professional Education Director. MCTC has 33,000 square feet of meeting space and assists with set-ups, exhibits, educational event gatherings, catering, and printing s... View Details Bookmark Assistant Director, Member Services and Student Employment 24 - Division of Academic and Student Affairs 244040 - Wellness and Recreation EPS/SAAO No NC State University is seeking an energetic, innovative, and student-centered leader to serve as the Assistant Director of Member Services and Student Employment. We are looking for a collaborative, proven leader who thrives in a fast-paced, results-oriented environment and is passionate about student success. The ideal candidate will empower both student and professional staff to cultivate wor... View Details Bookmark Budget Analyst 20 - Poole College of Management 200101 - Dean's Office - Poole College Of Management EPS/SAAO No The Budget Analyst provides professional budget and financial support to the Poole College Office of Business Services (OBS). Reporting to the Finance Officer, the position assists academic and administrative units with budget development, financial monitoring, and reporting to support effective fiscal management. As, the Budget Analyst you will analyze financial data, prepares budget reports, ... View Details Bookmark Research Technician (Lab and Field) - DEPP 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 111801 - Entomology and Plant Pathology SHRA No This position plays a key role in planning and executing research protocols, collecting and analyzing data, maintaining research materials, and contributing to scientific reports and project outcomes. The Research Technician will coordinate, conduct, and oversee research activities supporting laboratory and field-based experiments. The Research Technician will also lead research support activit... View Details Bookmark Research Security Specialist 51 - Office of Information Technology (OIT) 511001 - Security & Compliance EPS/SAAO No Professional Knowledge The IT Security Professional provides technical implementations and daily monitoring of the university’s complex IT environment in accordance with best practices and standards such as NIST 800-171, CMMC, CUI, NIST 800-53, PCI DSS (Payment Card Industry Data Security Standards), DMCA, FERPA, GLBA, HIPAA, , etc. Responsibilities include cybersecurity reviews, risk assessmen... View Details Bookmark Extension Agent, 4-H (Assistant, Associate or Full Agent) 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 117624 - South Central District - Gaston NC Cooperative Extension No As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. What we offer: Health Insurance, Tuition waiver for university coursework, Attend non-revenue-generating sporting events for free.  Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare discounts, Wellness & Recreation Membership, and Wellness Programs that aim to build a th... View Details Bookmark Research Technician 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 110901 - Crop and Soil Sciences SHRA No Join the Cotton Genetics and Breeding Lab and contribute to research that advances cotton genetics, genomics, and plant breeding. As a Research Technician, you will provide essential technical and operational support across field, greenhouse, growth chamber, laboratory, and seed-processing environments. Working alongside faculty, graduate students, postdoctoral researchers, and collaborators, y... View Details Bookmark Business Officer 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 115004 - Mountain Horticultural Crops Research EPS/SAAO No Reporting to the NC Agricultural Research Service, The Business Officer supports the administrative, financial, and operational success of the Mountain Horticultural Crops Research and Extension Center (MHCREC) and Mountain Horticultural Crops Research Station (MHCRS). In this highly collaborative role, you will help ensure research, extension, and outreach programs have the resources, faciliti... View Details Bookmark IT System Administrator 51 - Office of Information Technology (OIT) 517101 - Shared Services EPS/SAAO No As a member of the AWS team, you will bridge the gap between business needs and technology. You will work closely with application development teams to identify areas for process improvement and implement efficient solutions to meet business requirements. Using your technical and business knowledge to integrate and analyze data from multiple sources to draw conclusions and make recommendations,... View Details Bookmark Community Access Clinical Veterinarian 19 - College of Veterinary Medicine (CVM) 192001 - CVM Teaching Hospital EPS/SAAO No Are you passionate about breaking down barriers to veterinary care? We are seeking a dedicated Clinical Veterinarian to lead our mobile outreach initiative. This role is designed for a clinician who thrives on variety, enjoys community engagement, and is committed to providing high-quality primary care to underserved populations.The MissionAs part of our Community Access team, you will bring th... View Details Bookmark Small Animal Internal Medicine (SAIM) Fellowship 19 - College of Veterinary Medicine (CVM) 195001 - Department of Clinical Sciences Post Doc No The Small Animal Internal Medicine Service at the NC State Veterinary Hospital is seeking a highly motivated veterinarian for a one to two-year Small Animal Internal Medicine Fellowship. This program is specifically designed for individuals pursuing an academic career path, providing a bridge between residency training and a faculty role. Candidates will engage in advanced clinical service and ... View Details Bookmark Postdoctoral Research Scholar 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 110901 - Crop and Soil Sciences Post Doc No The Department of Crop and Soil Sciences encompasses varied disciplines in research, extension, and teaching. The department’s mission is to develop future leaders in crop, soil and environmental sciences, improve crop plants and products, devise effective and sustainable crop production systems, devise effective and sustainable soil management techniques in both agriculture and urban settings;... View Details Bookmark Clinical Research Technician – Small Animal Surgery 19 - College of Veterinary Medicine (CVM) 195001 - Department of Clinical Sciences SHRA No Join a collaborative clinical and surgical research team dedicated to advancing veterinary medicine through high-quality research. Working with Dr. Bae and Dr. McPhetridge, the Research Technician provides critical technical, administrative, and operational support that helps ensure the successful execution of multiple active research studies. This position plays an integral role in coordinatin... View Details Bookmark Market Supervisor 47 - Campus Enterprises 471501 - Dining Administration Temporary No Are you a natural leader with a passion for hospitality, team building, and great food? Step up as a Temporary Market Supervisor with NC State Dining!In this role, you’ll do more than manage day-to-day market operations—you’ll set the tone for exceptional campus service, coach a dynamic crew, and gain valuable management experience with one of North Carolina’s premier university dining programs... View Details Bookmark Emergency Reflief Veterinarian 19 - College of Veterinary Medicine (CVM) 190101 - College Of Veterinary Medicine Temporary No Emergency duties include being a primary emergency receiving clinician managing primary/referral emegency cases while mentoring and instructing house officers and senior veterinary students. View Details Bookmark Temporary Research Technician 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 110901 - Crop and Soil Sciences Temporary No Support the Small Grains and Official Variety Trial programs by assisting with seed processing, seed inventory, and plot preparation for the 2026–2027 research season. Responsibilities include counting and processing seed, collecting and managing research data, and maintaining accurate records throughout the growing season.Conduct field visits to monitor and document trial conditions, collect a... View Details Bookmark Temporary IT Intern - My Open Math 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 110201 - Agricultural Institute - Admin Temporary No The successful candidate will serve as the primary liaison between the AGI Math Lecturer and the MathGPT development team to support the successful implementation and ongoing use of the MathGPT platform within the mathematics curriculum.10Prior to the start of the Fall 2026 semester, the individual will be responsible for integrating the MAA 102 curriculum into MathGPT, importing course homewor... View Details Bookmark Temporary Research Assistant 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 111801 - Entomology and Plant Pathology Temporary No The successful candidate will conduct research to evaluate gene drive systems for the suppression of the New World screwworm. Responsibilities include designing, planning, conducting, and interpreting genetic experiments in consultation with Dr. Scott. The individual will collaborate closely with other members of the screwworm gene drive research team, including Dr. Yadav and Ms. Belikoff, to a... View Details Bookmark Temporary Event Technician Pool, University Theatre, Backstage & Front of House 24 - Division of Academic and Student Affairs 248901 - University Theatre Temporary No The Division of Academic & Student Affairs (DASA) is where students discover connections and community. It is where students live, where they gather, where they improve themselves, each other, and their university. DASA is where students seek