ity (NC State) is seeking a highly motivated and innovative individual for a tenure-track position at the level of Assistant Professor as part of the FRIB Experimental Bridge program. This unique position provides an exceptional opportunity for a dynamic researcher to thrive in a collaborative environment at the forefront of nuclear science.In this role, your profess... View Details Bookmark ICU Veterinary Assistant 19 - College of Veterinary Medicine (CVM) 192001 - CVM Teaching Hospital SHRA No The Intensive Care Unit (ICU) Veterinary Assistant provides advanced nursing care within the 24/7 high-acuity unit of the Randall B. Terry Jr. Companion Animal Medical Center. Operating in a fast-paced teaching environment, this role manages a varied caseload of small animal and exotic patients. The position requires a high level of clinical expertise, professional communication, and the abilit... View Details Bookmark Business Services Coordinator 14 - College of Engineering 141101 - Nuclear Engineering SHRA No The Department of Nuclear Engineering is seeking a highly organized and customer-focused professional to serve as a key member of its Business Office. In this role, you will support both the department and the Nuclear Reactor Program (NRP) by coordinating business operations, managing financial and administrative processes, and serving as a trusted resource for faculty, staff, students, and ext... View Details Bookmark Postdoctoral Research Scholar- Bioelectricity Lab 19 - College of Veterinary Medicine (CVM) 194001 - Department of Molecular Biomedical Sciences Post Doc No The Department of Molecular Biomedical Sciences trains doctors of veterinary medicine, graduate students, and postdoctoral fellows interested in research-based careers focused on discovering new information about animal and human health and disease and using those findings to enhance animal and human health and well-being.The Bioelectricity Lab develops next generation technologies for the dete... 