esProper set up and break down of bars. Setup events, work the event, and clean up after the event, including removing all catering items from the event space(s), washing any dirty catering items and... View Details Bookmark Lecturer - Applied Music Lecturers 24 - Division of Academic and Student Affairs 248401 - Performing Arts and Technology Non-Tenure-Track Faculty No The Performing Arts and Technology department at North Carolina State University seeks applications for applied music lecturers in all instrument areas to provide individual instruction for students who register for applied lessons. Responsibilities include teaching 13 weekly, 45-minute lessons per student and participation in the end–of–semester juried exams. This position is part-time; the ti... View Details Bookmark Open Rank Non-Tenure Track in Landscape Architecture & Environmental Planning 12 - College of Design 120401 - Landscape Architecture Non-Tenure-Track Faculty No The Department of LAEP is accepting applications for part-time non-tenure-track faculty appointments for a one-semester or one-year appointment with the possibility of renewal. Rank to be determined based upon education and professional experience.Specific teaching opportunities include landscape architecture and environmental planning studios at all levels, including advanced comprehensive stu... View Details Bookmark Open Rank Non Tenure Track in School of Architecture 12 - College of Design 120201 - Architecture Non-Tenure-Track Faculty No The School of Architecture is accepting applications for part-time non-tenure-track faculty appointments for a one-semester or one-year appointment with the possibility of renewal. Rank to be determined based on education and professional experience.Specific teaching opportunities include architecture studios at all levels, including advanced comprehensive studios and/or special topic seminar c... View Details Bookmark Open Rank Non Tenure Track in Media Arts, Design and Technology 12 - College of Design 120501 - Art and Design Non-Tenure-Track Faculty No The Department of Media Arts, Design and Technology is accepting applications for part-time non-tenure-track faculty appointments for a one-semester or one-year appointment with the possibility of renewal.Rank to be determined based upon education and professional experience. Specific teaching opportunities include art studios at all levels, including advanced comprehensive studios and/or speci... View Details Bookmark Open Rank Non-Tenure Track Teaching Positions - Graphic Design, Experience Design & Industrial Design 12 - College of Design 120301 - Graphic & Industrial Design Non-Tenure-Track Faculty No The Department of Graphic Design and Industrial Design is accepting applications for part-time non-tenure-track faculty appointments for one-semester, one-year, two-year, or three-year appointments, with the possibility of renewal. Positions encompass the following, with rank to be determined based on education and professional experience: Lecturer, Senior Lecturer, Assistant Teaching Professor... View Details Bookmark Lecturer - Biomedical Program 14 - College of Engineering 147501 - Lampe Joint Department of BME Non-Tenure-Track Faculty No Delivery of lectures that cover the course objectives as stated on the course syllabus following the dates of the NCSU university calendar for the given semester.Assessment of student performance including exams, projects, laboratory assignments and/or homework assignments as outlined on the course syllabus.If the course contains a lab section, overseeing the laboratory component to include:• S... View Details Bookmark Catering Event Supervisor 47 - Campus Enterprises 471501 - Dining Administration Temporary No Rave! Catering is seeking enthusiastic individuals to Join our Pack as a Catering Events Supervisor. Rave! Catering proudly employs experienced, certified chefs and catering professionals to provide the highest degree of service possible to ensure successful events.The primary purpose of this position is to supervise the prep work and setup for catering events around campus. Essential job dutie... View Details Bookmark Facilities Enhancement Technician 47 - Campus Enterprises 477001 - Student Centers Operations Temporary No We are seeking enthusiastic individuals to Join our Pack as a temporary Facilities Enhancement Technician. The Student Centers Facilities Enhancement team offers meaningful opportunities for employment across our retail and hospitality units. We offer flexible schedules and opportunities for learning, growth, and promotion. Dedicated and experienced professional staff are available to provide o... View Details Bookmark Postdoctoral Research Scholar 14 - College of Engineering 140801 - Materials Science &Engineering Post Doc No The Kinga Unocic Research Group in the Department of Materials Science andEngineering at North Carolina State University is seeking a Postdoctoral ResearchScholar to start December 2024. The Postdoc Research Scholars’ primary duties willinclude performing high-temperature oxidation testing, characterization of oxidationcoupons, and assisting with the lab setup.Other Duties and ResponsibilitiesA... View Details Bookmark Research Assistant 06 - Office of Research and Innovation 062001 - Institute For Transportation Research & Education Temporary No This position, up to 40 hours per week, will support research activities within the Research Group at ITRE primarily in the areas of roadway monitoring and roadway modeling, among others. This position will assist with research tasks related to monitoring roadways for safety and operations, as well as modeling roadway networks and processing and analyzing data. Additional tasks may be assigned ... View Details Bookmark Temporary Project YES Staff Intern 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 111401 - Agricultural and Human Sciences Temporary No Project YES interns provide youth development programs for children and youth of military families impacted by military deployments. Programs may be delivered during Yellow Ribbon Reintegration Program (YRRP) events (any phase) throughout the United States and all US territories.  Staff interns are not required to be North Carolina State University students. Interns remain at their home univers... View Details Bookmark Temporary-Professional NonFaculty 06 - Office of Research and Innovation 062001 - Institute For Transportation Research & Education Temporary No This position, up to 29 hours per week, will support research activities within the Research Group at ITRE primarily in the areas of roadway monitoring and roadway modeling, among others. This position will assist with research tasks related to web-mapping applications, as well as updating all Python scripts. Additional tasks may be assigned to this position in other relevant areas, based on th... View Details Bookmark Driver 39 - Office of Global Engagement 390701 – Global Training Initiative Temporary No The person in this role will help with airport pick-up/drop-off as well as scheduled events for NC State international visitors participating in a GTI and other international program. The selected candidate will transport program participants to/from their temporary accommodations, training locations, and other scheduled activities. The selected candidate must have flexibility in availability a... View Details Bookmark Assistant/Associate/Full Clinical or Tenure Track Professor of Radiation Oncology 19 - College of Veterinary Medicine (CVM) 195001 - Department of Clinical Sciences Non-Tenure-Track Faculty No The individual will be able to choose between either a TENURE TRACK or PROFESSIONAL/CLINICAL TRACK position, provided they meet the qualifications, with rank and tenure status determined based on experience level.Both positions come with similar responsibilities: the incumbent will oversee radiation oncology clinical case management, provide high quality clinical and pre-clinical teaching, demo... View Details Bookmark Fire/Life Safety Special Events - Fire Watch 42 - Environmental Health & Public Safety 427201 -  Fire and Life Safety Temporary No Perform fire watch and assist with life safety programs at special events, to include sporting events. Respond to fire related incidents as requested. View Details Bookmark Postdoctoral Research Scholar 14 - College of Engineering 140301 - Civil Construction & Environmental Engineering Post Doc No NC State Department of Civil, Construction, and Environmental Engineering (CCEE), seeks a postdoctoral researcher in the transportation area related to human-Autonomous Vehicle (AV) interactions. For questions regarding the position please contact Professor Danjue Chen (dchen33@ncsu.edu).The postdoc training and mentoring will be in:1. Helping to advance research in human-automation interaction... View Details Bookmark Linux Desktop Support 14 - College of Engineering 140401 - Electrical & Computer Engineering Exempt Professional Staff No We are seeking a highly skilled Linux Desktop Support professional to join our team and take charge of the hardware and software administration for our growing (200+) fleet of desktops, workstations, and laptops running RedHat Enterprise Linux and Ubuntu Linux. As a Linux Desktop Support Professional, you will be responsible for ensuring the smooth operation and optimal performance of our Linux... View Details Bookmark C:LAB Makerspace Technician 24 - Division of Academic and Student Affairs 243030 - Crafts Center Temporary No The Division of Academic & Student Affairs (DASA) is where students discover connections and community. It is where students live, where they gather, where they improve themselves, each other, and their university. DASA is where students seek guidance and support, both in and outside of the classroom. The division serves all students at NC State through three integrated components: academic... View Details Bookmark Temporary-Professional NonFaculty 14 - College of Engineering 140901 - Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering Temporary No This posting is for the hiring of a variety of Professional non-faculty positions for short-term hire’s, that are needed in various areas of specific topics on an as-needed basis in the department. . Areas include Laboratory research and support for academic course development. This position stays open year-round to assist in various as-needed temporary hires. View Details Bookmark Master Police Officer I - III 42 - Environmental Health & Public Safety 425001 - Police Department State Law Enforcement (EPS) No The main purpose of the NC State University Master Officer position is to protect and serve the students, faculty, staff and visitors of North Carolina State University through law enforcement and crime prevention. The selected candidate(s) will patrol campus and investigate complaints and violations of State laws and local ordinances. This person also develops and implements preventative patro... View Details Bookmark UTS - Temporary Electronics Specialist at UNC Chapel Hill (2nd Shift) 48 - Human Resources 480502 - UHR UTS/UNC Partnership Temporary No This position serves as part of the Life Safety/Electronics-Specialty Shop team, ensuring the smooth operation of critical safety and monitoring systems across campus. The role involves both preventive maintenance and hands-on installations or modifications to essential systems that support the safety, security, and functionality of the university.As an Electronics Specialist, you will perform ... View Details Bookmark Police Officer 42 - Environmental Health & Public Safety 425001 - Police Department State Law Enforcement (EPS) No The main purpose of the NC State University Police Officer position is to protect and serve the students, faculty, staff and visitors of North Carolina State University through law enforcement and crime prevention. The selected candidate(s) will patrol campus and investigate complaints and violations of State laws and local ordinances. This person also develops and implements preventative patro... View Details Bookmark Temporary Internship Program Assistant 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 111502 - Center for Environmental Farming Systems (CEFS) Temporary No Supporting with the overall coordination, including logistics, administration, planning professional development and evaluation of the summer internships for the Center for Environmental Farming Systems.Specific duties include:Internship recruitingPlanning and coordinating logistics or professional developmentTracking and documenting activitiesAssist with paying farmersSupport interns with day-... View Details Bookmark LAS Intern 06 - Office of Research and Innovation 061801 - Lab for Analytical Sciences Temporary No The Laboratory of Analytic Sciences (LAS) requires an intern to complete research in the areas of interest to LAS. Potential areas of research include but are not limited to: social sciences, applied sciences and engineering.This posting will remain open as we hire interns throughout the year from institutions other than NC State University. View Details Bookmark Temp Project Youth Extension Service Staff Intern 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 111401 - Agricultural and Human Sciences Temporary No Project YES interns provide youth development programs for children and youth of military families throughout the United States and US territories.  Programs may be delivered during Yellow Ribbon events (any phase) and other youth centric activities, i.e. councils, leadership summits, family days, camps, etc.  Staff interns are not required to be North Carolina State University students.  Inter... View Details Bookmark LTAP Coordinator 06 - Office of Research and Innovation 062001 - Institute For Transportation Research & Education Temporary No This position, up to 30 hours per week, will support LTAP activities at ITRE:Complete data entry for Excel and Access database which LTAP uses to track class registrations, attendance, payments and other essential information that is required for a successful training programPrepare communications to promote classes to listserv and on social mediaAssist in preparing the quarterly newsletterTrav... View Details Bookmark Deputy General Counsel 27 - Office of General Counsel 270101 - Office of General Counsel Exempt Professional Staff (Previously SAAO II) No The Deputy General Counsel plays a pivotal role in advancing the university’s mission by providing high-level legal counsel and strategic guidance on matters impacting North Carolina State University. As a trusted advisor and key member of the Office of General Counsel leadership team, this position reports directly to the Vice Chancellor and General Counsel.The Deputy General Counsel will coll... View Details Bookmark Previous 1 2 … 6 7 8 9 10 11 12 13 14 Next NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
