h integrated communications, digital media, and desktop IT services. The role delivers specialized expertise in social media, accessibility‑compliant communications, website maintenance, event support, and frontline IT troubleshooting for faculty, staff, and students. This position ensures con... View Details Bookmark LAS Intern 06 - Office of Research and Innovation 061801 - Lab for Analytical Sciences Temporary No The Laboratory of Analytic Sciences (LAS) requires an intern to complete research in the areas of interest to LAS. Potential areas of research include but are not limited to: social sciences, applied sciences and engineering.This posting will remain open as we hire interns throughout the year from institutions other than NC State University. View Details Bookmark Research Scholar 06 - Office of Research and Innovation 062001 - Institute For Transportation Research & Education Temporary No The School Planning and Transportation group supports Local Education Authorities (LEAs) in comprehensive planning for schools and communities (SchoolCAMP), enrollment, facilities and boundary planning (OREd) and school transportation (Bike/Ped, Transit, School Bus). This position will support multiple initiatives at ITRE that support local, state and national Public Pre-Kindergarten to 12 th g... View Details Bookmark LTAP Coordinator 06 - Office of Research and Innovation 062001 - Institute For Transportation Research & Education Temporary No This position, up to 30 hours per week, will support LTAP activities at ITRE:Complete data entry for Excel and Access database which LTAP uses to track class registrations, attendance, payments and other essential information that is required for a successful training programPrepare communications to promote classes to listserv and on social mediaAssist in preparing the quarterly newsletterTrav... View Details Bookmark Temporary-Professional NonFaculty 06 - Office of Research and Innovation 062001 - Institute For Transportation Research & Education Temporary No This position, up to 29 hours per week, will support research activities within the Research Group at ITRE primarily in the areas of roadway monitoring and roadway modeling, among others. This position will assist with research tasks related to web-mapping applications, as well as updating all Python scripts. Additional tasks may be assigned to this position in other relevant areas, based on th... View Details Bookmark Research Assistant 06 - Office of Research and Innovation 062001 - Institute For Transportation Research & Education Temporary No This position, up to 40 hours per week, will support research activities within the Research Group at ITRE primarily in the areas of roadway monitoring and roadway modeling, among others. This position will assist with research tasks related to monitoring roadways for safety and operations, as well as modeling roadway networks and processing and analyzing data. Additional tasks may be assigned ... View Details Bookmark Postdoctoral Research Scholar 06 - Office of Research and Innovation 063001 - NC Institute of Climate Studies Post Doc No Duties and Responsibilities:The Postdoctoral Research Scholar will be working in the area of compounding and cascading extreme weather events.Research tasks include statistical analysis of historical observations and model simulations of compounding events and evaluation of data-driven earth system model simulations for compounding events.The postdoc researcher will support multiple NOAA and NS... View Details Bookmark Associate Vice Chancellor, Research Commercialization 06 - Office of Research and Innovation 067401 - ORC - Technology Licensing Office EPS/SAAO No The Associate Vice Chancellor for Research Commercialization (AVC‑RC) provides executive leadership for NC State’s commercialization enterprise, spanning intellectual property management, licensing, startup formation, venture development, and investment programs. The AVC sets university‑wide commercialization strategy, ensures compliance with federal and institutional requirements, and leads pr... View Details Bookmark Executive Director of Gift Planning 08 - University Advancement 082001 - University Development EPS/SAAO No Reporting to the Assistant Vice Chancellor for University Development, the Executive Director for Gift Planning serves as the university’s senior leader for gift planning, providing strategic direction, oversight, and execution of a comprehensive, campus-wide program. The Executive Director partners across Advancement to integrate gift planning into fundraising strategy, supports complex and de... View Details Bookmark Director of Creative Media & Content Strategy 10 - Athletics 101012 - Football EPS/SAAO Yes Serve as the primary creative director responsible for overseeing all creative content (video, photography, graphic design, social media) ideation, creation, and delivery strategies for the football program.Responsibilities and duties include but are not limited to:Coordinates the creative direction, ideation, plans, estimates and timetables for football contentCreation and distribution on soci... View Details Bookmark Production Assistant - Temp 10 - Athletics 105002 - Athletics - Internal/External Operations Temporary No Serve as camera operator to work live broadcasts and in-house productions for NC State University Athletics (football, basketball, baseball, soccer, etc.) in Raleigh, NC. Experience with live camera work in sports is highly preferable but not necessary. Other production positions (Graphics, Replay, TD, etc.) are a possibility too based on experience. Help during set up and tear down before and ... View Details Bookmark Ticket Office Operations Assistant 10 - Athletics 105002 - Athletics - Internal/External Operations Temporary No The NC State Athletics Ticket Office is a division of the Athletic Department at NC State University and is responsible for all ticket operations at sporting events hosted by NC State Athletics. Ticket operations include the following sports: football, men’s and women’s basketball, volleyball, baseball, softball, wrestling, and gymnastics. Ticket Office employees will be responsible for providi... View Details Bookmark Assistant Engineer 10 - Athletics 105002 - Athletics - Internal/External Operations SHRA No NC State Athletics is a leader in video and broadcast production, supporting high-profile live events and innovative media experiences across its athletic venues. We are seeking a Broadcast Engineering professional to join our team and help ensure the reliable operation and delivery of complex productions across the department.Reporting to the Director of Engineering, this position plays a hand... View Details Bookmark Game Operations Assistant (Temp) 10 - Athletics 107005 - Athletics - Game Operations Temporary No Game Operations Assistants provide support to Facilities & Operation staff in maintaining and operating all NC State Athletics facilities and game-day events.Responsibilities:• Complete game-day operations tasks as assigned including assisting with customer service to patrons, ingress and egress of events, serving as a liaison for the athletics department to various guest personnel, etc.• A... View Details Bookmark Career Counselor, CALS Career Services 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 110101 - CALS - Academic Programs EPS/SAAO No The Career Counselor will enhance the career and professional development of CALS students through individual career counseling and training programs. The Career Counselor’s work will contribute to 4,500+ CALS students improving their career readiness, participating in experiential learning, and securing post-graduation opportunities aligning with their interests. The person in this position wi... View Details Bookmark Career Services Coordinator, CALS Career Services 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 110101 - CALS - Academic Programs EPS/SAAO No The Career Services Coordinator will enhance the career and professional development of CALS students through overseeing the CALS Alumni for Student Success (CASS) Career Coach program and providing programmatic support to all functions of the CALS Career Services office. The Coordinator’s work will contribute to 4,500+ CALS students improving their career readiness, participating in experienti... View Details Bookmark Director of Philanthropy 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 110199 - Agriculture Related Foundation Exempt Professional Staff No The Director of Philanthropy is responsible for identifying, qualifying, soliciting, and stewarding major gift donors to NC State University. This position will serve as a member of the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences (CALS) Advancement team, reporting to a Senior Director of Philanthropy with an effort to maximize support to all areas of the College. As appropriate, the Director will ... View Details Bookmark Temporary IT Intern - My Open Math 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 110201 - Agricultural Institute - Admin Temporary No The successful candidate will serve as the primary liaison between the AGI Math Lecturer and the MathGPT development team to support the successful implementation and ongoing use of the MathGPT platform within the mathematics curriculum.10Prior to the start of the Fall 2026 semester, the individual will be responsible for integrating the MAA 102 curriculum into MathGPT, importing course homewor... View Details Bookmark Financial Operations Supervisor 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 110305 - CALS Business Office EPS/SAAO No As the Financial Operations Supervisor, you will serve as a strategic financial anchor within the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences (CALS), providing direct leadership and accounting oversight for a centralized financial operations team. Reporting to the Director of Business Services, you will safeguard the integrity, accuracy, and compliance of high-risk transactions across a complex mu... View Details Bookmark Temporary Financial Operations Specialist 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 110305 - CALS Business Office Temporary No The Temporary Financial Operations Specialist provides accounting and financial operations support within the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences (CALS) Business Services unit. Business Services is transitioning to a cross-functional service model in which employees develop proficiency across multiple financial operations functions. Employees will support Accounts Payable, Accounts Receiva... View Details Bookmark Postdoctoral Research Scholar - PHHI 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 110308 - Kannapolis Research Post Doc No The Postdoctoral Scholar will assist the Principal Investigator (Dr. Andrew Neilson) in the Plants for Human Health Institute by leading and conducting independent research (80%), along with some general laboratory management (10%), and some mentoring of graduate students as appropriate (10%).Duties and Responsibilities:The primary duties of this position will include conducting advanced indepe... View Details Bookmark Research Technician - PHHI 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 110308 - Kannapolis Research SHRA No The Komarnytsky Lab, part of the Plants for Human Health Institute and Department of Food, Bioprocessing, and Nutrition Sciences, has developed an integrated translational pipeline linking molecular insights from cell culture and animal models to physiological outcomes in clinical settings, with special focus on metabolic resilience, pharmacogenomics, optimized physical performance, and innovat... View Details Bookmark Temporary Research Technician - Kannapolis, NC 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 110308 - Kannapolis Research Temporary No The position will support the operations at the Human Performance Laboratory located at the North Carolina Research Campus. This role is vital for executing clinical research and community fitness testing by conducting specialized procedures. The research technician is responsible for ensuring quality control during data collection, conducting subject recruitment and scheduling, and maintaining... View Details Bookmark Temporary Research Specialist - Kannapolis, NC 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 110308 - Kannapolis Research Temporary No 1. Oversee trial evaluation for disease in carrot. This task will require some travel to the research station in Clinton on a weekly base. 2.  Manage in vitro culture material 3. Perform routine laboratory duties including molecular biology assays (DNA extraction, PCR, real time) View Details Bookmark Temporary NCFIL Intern - Kannapolis, NC 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 110309 - NC Food Innovation Lab Temporary No Assist in product development of plant-based beverages, meat substitutes, bakery and confections; scale up and product commercialization of both food &amp; beverage ingredients and finished products; develop standard operating procedures, research current and future processing techniques, perform quality testing and shelf life studies on food samples, assist in ordering and stocking ingredi... View Details Bookmark Swine Extension Program Associate 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 110701 - Animal Science SHRA No The North Carolina State University Department of Animal Science is seeking a Swine Extension Program Associate. This position will be primarily responsible for working with NCSU scientists to develop and deliver swine educational opportunities throughout North Carolina and beyond Specific extension programming efforts include organizing, managing, and assisting with NCSU Swine Innovation Forum... View Details Bookmark Research Technician 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 110701 - Animal Science SHRA No Support innovative research in reproductive physiology and molecular biology by providing technical expertise and laboratory support for multiple research programs. As a Research Technician, you will play an essential role in maintaining transgenic mouse colonies, conducting molecular biology experiments, and supporting faculty, students, and scientists in advancing high-quality research. This ... View Details Bookmark Microbiology Laboratory Research Technician 11 - College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) 110801 - Plant & Microbial Biology SHRA No The Kleiner Lab at North Carolina State University is seeking a Research Technician to support research focused on complex microbial communities, microbial symbioses, and metaproteomics. Reporting to the Kleiner Lab research team, this position contributes to the design, execution, and analysis of experiments that advance the lab’s research program and generate findings for publications, confer... View Details Bookmark Previous 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9 … 13 14 Next NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
