    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234706": {
      "title": "NCSU Employment Site | UTS - Temporary Radiology Technician at NC State",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | UTS - Temporary Radiology Technician at NC State Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) UTS - Temporary Radiology Technician at NC State Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG196132TM Position Number 48AJ40 Position Type Temporary Essential Job Duties The primary duties of this position include the following: Taking X-ray images of the human body per order by provider. Interact with internal staff, patients, and referring providers through email, phone, and in-person communications. Keeping equipment clean and in working order. Responsible for maintaining equipment and quality control. Attend scheduled meetings, drills, and training. Perform technical procedures, including patient positioning for radiographs and digital image capturing. Provide excellent patient care by applying full knowledge of anatomy, physiology, and disease processes. Provide quick and accurate information regarding each patient, acting as a liaison between clinicians and radiologists. Proficiently enter data into the electronic health record. Maintain a clean working environment to ensure standards are followed and infection is not spread. Handle medical, biological, and infectious waste appropriately. Follow all radiation safety, OSHA , and Environmental Health and Safety standards. Is Time Limited Yes If Yes, Appointment Length 6 or more months Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here , and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Health Insurance for Temporary Employees Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare discounts , Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Department Information Job City & State Raleigh, NC Department System Information Classification Title Temporary-Technical/Paraprofessional Working Title UTS - Temporary Radiology Technician at NC State Position Information Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule 8:00 am – 5:00 pm, Monday – Friday Other Work/Responsibilities Other duties as assigned Minimum Experience/Education -Graduate from Radiology Program - ARRT certification. Department Required Skills Experience with Electronic Health Records software. Must be able to lift up to 60 pounds occasionally, with or without reasonable accommodations. Skilled in the use of radiology equipment and in the performance of procedures. Ability to work independently and practice good judgment to ensure high-quality care. Ability to perform specialized orthopedic procedures such as weight-bearing lower extremities. CPR certification (can also obtain during position) ARRT certification. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education EHS Software skills Radiology imaging skills Required License or Certification -Graduate from Radiology Program - ARRT certification Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $32.00 an hour Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 07/30/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/233332 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu. Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about UTS? (Open Ended Question) * Do you currently hold a valid American Registry of Radiologic Technologists (ARRT) certification? Yes No, I do not. * Do you possess a current CPR certification, or are you willing and able to obtain one prior to or upon hire? Yes, currently certified. No, but willing to obtain upon hire No * Are you comfortable with the physical requirements of this role, including lifting, positioning, or moving up to 60 pounds occasionally, with or without a reasonable accommodation? Yes, I am. No, I am not. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Contact Information for References Optional Documents Cover Letter NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
